1
00:00:07,000 --> 00:00:10,000
[Bloster] All right,
how many are there?

2
00:00:10,000 --> 00:00:12,000
[Welfin] Right around 5,000,

3
00:00:12,000 --> 00:00:15,000
and that's only about a fifth
of the quota we're aiming for.

4
00:00:15,000 --> 00:00:18,000
[Bloster] The King
must be pretty ticked off.

5
00:00:23,000 --> 00:00:25,000
He plays so much Gungi
that he barely eats.

6
00:00:38,000 --> 00:00:40,000
only after you get a taste yourself.

7
00:00:41,000 --> 00:00:44,000
I'll do whatever those monsters tell me.

8
00:00:44,000 --> 00:00:46,000
[Welfin] I bet Sir Shaia anticipated

9
00:00:46,000 --> 00:00:49,000
things would turn out like this
when he gave us our abilities.

10
00:00:52,000 --> 00:00:57,000
He gets mad if you call him
by his old name now.

11
00:00:57,000 --> 00:01:00,000
[opening theme music playing]

12
00:01:32,000 --> 00:01:36,000
[singer singing in English]

13
00:01:42,000 --> 00:01:46,000
[singer singing in Japanese]

14
00:01:59,000 --> 00:02:00,000
[singer singing in English]

15
00:02:00,000 --> 00:02:04,000
[singer singing in Japanese]

16
00:02:43,000 --> 00:02:45,000
[Leol] And his abilities?

17
00:02:45,000 --> 00:02:46,000
[Flutter] Much like the others,

18
00:02:46,000 --> 00:02:50,000
he's used only physical attacks thus far.

19
00:02:50,000 --> 00:02:52,000
[Leol] Okay. Just let me know
if he reveals his abilities.

20
00:02:55,000 --> 00:02:57,000
Once Welfin and Bloster arrive,

21
00:02:57,000 --> 00:03:00,000
we'll take care of those figures in white.

22
00:03:09,000 --> 00:03:12,000
[Flutter] Damn!
I lost sight of him.

23
00:03:12,000 --> 00:03:15,000
Sir Leol, it appears that
the man in the suit and glasses

24
00:03:15,000 --> 00:03:17,000
has the ability to teleport.

25
00:03:21,000 --> 00:03:24,000
[narrator] Knov's ability
is called hide-and-seek,

26
00:03:24,000 --> 00:03:27,000
and it does indeed allow him to teleport.

27
00:03:28,000 --> 00:03:31,000
By placing his hand
over a wall or on the ground,

28
00:03:31,000 --> 00:03:34,000
he can open a portal to a Nen dimension.

29
00:03:34,000 --> 00:03:37,000
What's more, he can then
send people or objects

30
00:03:37,000 --> 00:03:40,000
through that portal to the other side.

31
00:03:40,000 --> 00:03:46,000
Hide-and-seek creates a Nen dimension
of 21 rooms spread across four floors.

32
00:03:46,000 --> 00:03:49,000
Each room is completely
independent from the others.

33
00:03:52,000 --> 00:03:55,000
so in order to return
to the real world, one must exit

34
00:04:02,000 --> 00:04:05,000
but exactly how many
depends on the size of the room.

35
00:04:05,000 --> 00:04:07,000
The exit leads directly

36
00:04:07,000 --> 00:04:09,000
back to the portal
that was used for entry,

37
00:04:09,000 --> 00:04:13,000
so as a general rule,
one can only enter and exit

38
00:04:13,000 --> 00:04:16,000
via the location of the entry portal.

39
00:04:16,000 --> 00:04:19,000
However, the master key
in Knov's possession

40
00:04:19,000 --> 00:04:24,000
is able to connect any door
to any portal in any location.

41
00:04:32,000 --> 00:04:35,000
[distant gunfire echoing]

42
00:04:35,000 --> 00:04:39,000
[Knov] No change. All in good order.

43
00:04:40,000 --> 00:04:44,000
[narrator] Morel's Deep Purple
is primarily used for defense.

44
00:05:02,000 --> 00:05:05,000
the figures in white
avoid direct contact with their opponents,

45
00:05:05,000 --> 00:05:07,000
lest they betray their secret.

46
00:05:08,000 --> 00:05:09,000
[dramatic music playing]

47
00:05:09,000 --> 00:05:11,000
[Knov] That's a Chimera.

48
00:05:12,000 --> 00:05:14,000
But what's it doing here?

49
00:05:14,000 --> 00:05:17,000
We're pretty far from the battlefield.

50
00:05:17,000 --> 00:05:18,000
Is it scouting the area?

51
00:05:21,000 --> 00:05:24,000
There were strange dragonflies
around town.

52
00:05:24,000 --> 00:05:26,000
I thought they were a local species,

53
00:05:26,000 --> 00:05:28,000
but could they be products of his Nen?

54
00:05:29,000 --> 00:05:31,000
Seems likely.

55
00:05:31,000 --> 00:05:34,000
If it's a Chimera Ant that
specializes in gathering intel,

56
00:05:34,000 --> 00:05:38,000
I need to neutralize it, and quickly!

57
00:05:45,000 --> 00:05:48,000
[Cheetu] Hey! Hey!

58
00:05:58,000 --> 00:06:00,000
Whoa, there!

59
00:06:01,000 --> 00:06:03,000
I knew you were playing possum
all along.

60
00:06:03,000 --> 00:06:05,000
You can't trick me.

61
00:06:05,000 --> 00:06:07,000
I can't sleep
with all your damn racket!

62
00:06:21,000 --> 00:06:25,000
then you should have enforced rules
that would make people chase you.

63
00:06:26,000 --> 00:06:29,000
Looks like his new ability
still needs some work.

64
00:06:37,000 --> 00:06:40,000
[Morel] He's obsessed with
challenging me to a footrace.

65
00:06:41,000 --> 00:06:44,000
Between that and
his constant need for attention,

66
00:06:53,000 --> 00:06:56,000
Look! I'm over here! Don't you
wanna get up and grab me?

67
00:06:59,000 --> 00:07:02,000
[Morel] Now it's just a waiting game.

68
00:07:02,000 --> 00:07:06,000
As soon as he gives up
and steps away from me,

69
00:07:07,000 --> 00:07:08,000
I win.

70
00:07:09,000 --> 00:07:12,000
[thunder rumbling]

71
00:07:55,000 --> 00:07:56,000
[Champion] Mortar, two-seven-two.

72
00:08:05,000 --> 00:08:07,000
Fort, seven-one-two. Your move.

73
00:08:08,000 --> 00:08:10,000
All right then. Prince, one-six-two.

74
00:08:15,000 --> 00:08:18,000
[Champion] Captain, three-two-two.

75
00:08:18,000 --> 00:08:20,000
I'm finished.

76
00:08:20,000 --> 00:08:23,000
Her opening array is just as I expected.

77
00:08:24,000 --> 00:08:27,000
She's moving toward my King
while staying in wing formation.

78
00:08:28,000 --> 00:08:30,000
Now let us begin to play the game.

79
00:08:30,000 --> 00:08:33,000
[King] Her first move
will be to position her archer

80
00:08:33,000 --> 00:08:36,000
on her right flank
to threaten a trident attack,

81
00:08:37,000 --> 00:08:39,000
but shifting her pieces to the right

82
00:08:39,000 --> 00:08:42,000
exposes her left flank to attack.

83
00:08:44,000 --> 00:08:47,000
This time, I will disrupt your rhythm.

84
00:09:01,000 --> 00:09:03,000
[Champion] Cavalry, two-nine-one.

85
00:09:03,000 --> 00:09:06,000
[King] Her trident attack and
the movement of her left flank

86
00:09:17,000 --> 00:09:20,000
but instead, I'll do this!

87
00:09:21,000 --> 00:09:24,000
Duke, five-five-one.

88
00:09:32,000 --> 00:09:35,000
[Shaiapouf] She had been
playing with a consistent tempo,

89
00:09:35,000 --> 00:09:38,000
but now she's paused
for the first time.

90
00:09:38,000 --> 00:09:41,000
[King] When attacking
from this central placement,

91
00:09:41,000 --> 00:09:43,000
the possibilities are infinite.

92
00:09:43,000 --> 00:09:45,000
There are no correct moves.

93
00:09:53,000 --> 00:09:55,000
gasp for air!

94
00:10:03,000 --> 00:10:06,000
[ominous music playing]

95
00:10:14,000 --> 00:10:16,000
[Champion] New duke,
nine-two-one.

96
00:10:16,000 --> 00:10:18,000
[King gasps]

97
00:10:18,000 --> 00:10:21,000
[dramatic music playing]

98
00:10:28,000 --> 00:10:29,000
[King] I resign.

99
00:10:31,000 --> 00:10:35,000
You knew that this was
a dead end, didn't you?

100
00:10:36,000 --> 00:10:37,000
Yes.

101
00:10:37,000 --> 00:10:41,000
Then why did you pause to
think before making your move?

102
00:10:41,000 --> 00:10:44,000
You could have made it immediately.

103
00:10:44,000 --> 00:10:47,000
[Shaiapouf] The King has moved
this match off the board.

104
00:10:47,000 --> 00:10:51,000
A wrong answer could mean her death.

105
00:10:51,000 --> 00:10:53,000
[thunder rumbling]

106
00:10:53,000 --> 00:10:56,000
Actually sir,
this "detached castling" strategy

107
00:10:56,000 --> 00:11:01,000
you were using is more commonly
known as "Kokoriko."

108
00:11:12,000 --> 00:11:15,000
is also my novelty move,
called "Central duke."

109
00:11:16,000 --> 00:11:19,000
At the time, they both
drew a lot of attention.

110
00:11:19,000 --> 00:11:22,000
The sequence from "Kokoriko"
to "Central duke"

111
00:11:22,000 --> 00:11:25,000
was an excellent way to test
each other's level of insight.

112
00:11:25,000 --> 00:11:27,000
It was very popular.

113
00:11:28,000 --> 00:11:31,000
I was so happy that a fool
like me could still give birth

114
00:11:31,000 --> 00:11:33,000
to something that was so intelligent.

115
00:11:33,000 --> 00:11:36,000
I even called it "My smart little baby."

116
00:11:37,000 --> 00:11:40,000
But soon after that,
I found out how to kill it.

117
00:11:42,000 --> 00:11:44,000
A year after I came up with "Kokoriko,"

118
00:11:44,000 --> 00:11:48,000
an opponent used it against me
in the national title tournament,

119
00:11:48,000 --> 00:11:51,000
and I figured out this countermove,

120
00:11:52,000 --> 00:11:54,000
so I was able to win the match.

121
00:11:54,000 --> 00:11:56,000
But then it disappeared.

122
00:11:56,000 --> 00:12:00,000
You didn't see it in any more matches,
or even in textbooks.

123
00:12:00,000 --> 00:12:04,000
To think that you came up
with the same strategy I had,

124
00:12:04,000 --> 00:12:08,000
I was so honored and touched,

125
00:12:09,000 --> 00:12:11,000
so much so that my heart trembled.

126
00:12:12,000 --> 00:12:13,000
It felt like…

127
00:12:17,000 --> 00:12:20,000
seeing my dead baby come back to life.

128
00:12:23,000 --> 00:12:24,000
That's how it felt.

129
00:12:45,000 --> 00:12:46,000
[King scoffs]

130
00:12:46,000 --> 00:12:48,000
Rubbish.

131
00:12:48,000 --> 00:12:51,000
I've lost interest. Take a break.

132
00:12:51,000 --> 00:12:53,000
[Champion] Huh?

133
00:12:54,000 --> 00:12:57,000
-[King] Once we begin again--
-[Champion] Eh?

134
00:13:07,000 --> 00:13:09,000
[Shaiapouf]
I'm actually impressed.

135
00:13:09,000 --> 00:13:11,000
The King has never
listened to someone else

136
00:13:11,000 --> 00:13:14,000
for that long before, not nearly.

137
00:13:14,000 --> 00:13:18,000
Oh, well. It should
have no significance.

138
00:13:22,000 --> 00:13:23,000
[Morel] Four hours have passed?

139
00:13:29,000 --> 00:13:32,000
That guy's way too predictable.

140
00:13:40,000 --> 00:13:41,000
Wait. It's only half done.

141
00:13:41,000 --> 00:13:44,000
[laughs]
Not getting anxious, are you?

142
00:13:51,000 --> 00:13:53,000
[Morel] Didn't you notice?

143
00:13:53,000 --> 00:13:55,000
It's not time to begin.

144
00:13:55,000 --> 00:13:56,000
It's already over.

145
00:13:57,000 --> 00:13:59,000
Just take a look at your ankle.

146
00:13:59,000 --> 00:14:00,000
[Cheetu] Huh?

147
00:14:07,000 --> 00:14:09,000
I had to go all the way around

148
00:14:09,000 --> 00:14:11,000
so you wouldn't notice what I was doing.

149
00:14:11,000 --> 00:14:13,000
It turned to a pretty long rope.

150
00:14:13,000 --> 00:14:15,000
[Cheetu gasps]

151
00:14:20,000 --> 00:14:21,000
Won't be long now.

152
00:14:24,000 --> 00:14:26,000
[Cheetu growls]

153
00:14:29,000 --> 00:14:30,000
[laughs]

154
00:14:30,000 --> 00:14:33,000
Guess it's your turn to try
whatever you can think of,

155
00:14:33,000 --> 00:14:34,000
but don't expect it to work.

156
00:14:36,000 --> 00:14:38,000
[Cheetu gasps]

157
00:14:38,000 --> 00:14:39,000
[groans]

158
00:14:41,000 --> 00:14:43,000
Don't underestimate
the power of smoke.

159
00:14:43,000 --> 00:14:46,000
This rope's essentially unbreakable.

160
00:14:47,000 --> 00:14:49,000
Struggle all you want.

161
00:14:49,000 --> 00:14:51,000
[Cheetu growling]

162
00:15:00,000 --> 00:15:02,000
This is a game of tag,

163
00:15:03,000 --> 00:15:05,000
so he won't attack me.

164
00:15:05,000 --> 00:15:09,000
All I have to do is touch his body,
and it'll terminate his ability.

165
00:15:10,000 --> 00:15:13,000
He's the one who chose for
this game to last eight hours,

166
00:15:13,000 --> 00:15:16,000
even though he doesn't have
the attention span for it.

167
00:15:16,000 --> 00:15:18,000
I'm not your enemy here.

168
00:15:25,000 --> 00:15:28,000
but now that he finds himself cornered

169
00:15:28,000 --> 00:15:31,000
with nowhere to run and nowhere to hide…

170
00:15:31,000 --> 00:15:32,000
Huh?

171
00:15:32,000 --> 00:15:35,000
[narrator] He creates a new ability.

172
00:15:35,000 --> 00:15:38,000
[dramatic music playing]

173
00:15:43,000 --> 00:15:45,000
A crossbow and claws?

174
00:15:45,000 --> 00:15:46,000
[Cheetu chuckles]

175
00:15:46,000 --> 00:15:51,000
[Morel] Something for both close-range
and long-range combat.

176
00:15:51,000 --> 00:15:52,000
[laughs]

177
00:15:52,000 --> 00:15:53,000
Thanks a lot!

178
00:15:54,000 --> 00:15:56,000
You just helped me gain
an awesome new ability!

179
00:15:58,000 --> 00:16:00,000
See? Got any idea what it is?

180
00:16:07,000 --> 00:16:09,000
There!

181
00:16:19,000 --> 00:16:22,000
Why don't you
try out those claws already?

182
00:16:22,000 --> 00:16:25,000
It'll save me the trouble
of walking over there.

183
00:16:26,000 --> 00:16:30,000
I'll tell you why
you're gonna lose, because…

184
00:16:42,000 --> 00:16:44,000
[laughs]

185
00:16:44,000 --> 00:16:47,000
Come on! Just die,
so tagging me won't matter!

186
00:16:47,000 --> 00:16:51,000
Huh? This feels like…

187
00:17:05,000 --> 00:17:08,000
While you read your manga
and cackled to yourself,

188
00:17:17,000 --> 00:17:20,000
My copy went one way,
and I went the other.

189
00:17:20,000 --> 00:17:23,000
Sleeping doesn't mean
the fight just stops.

190
00:17:23,000 --> 00:17:25,000
You really should have
kept your eyes on me.

191
00:17:30,000 --> 00:17:32,000
Well? Still wanna fight?

192
00:17:40,000 --> 00:17:43,000
Maybe you'd be willing
to fill me in on a little something, then.

193
00:17:43,000 --> 00:17:45,000
Would you mind telling me
what would have happened

194
00:17:45,000 --> 00:17:49,000
if I hadn't caught you back there,
or do you know?

195
00:17:49,000 --> 00:17:50,000
[Cheetu] It doesn't matter anymore.

196
00:17:51,000 --> 00:17:54,000
Once I've been caught,
I can't use that ability ever again.

197
00:18:00,000 --> 00:18:02,000
[laughs] Oh, it's no big deal.

198
00:18:02,000 --> 00:18:05,000
I'll just ask Sir Shaia for a new ability!

199
00:18:06,000 --> 00:18:08,000
I won't lose next time!
Just you wait!

200
00:18:10,000 --> 00:18:12,000
[Morel] All right, then.

201
00:18:12,000 --> 00:18:16,000
So his superior is most likely
a royal guard named Shaia,

202
00:18:29,000 --> 00:18:30,000
[cell phone rings]

203
00:18:30,000 --> 00:18:33,000
[Knov] Let's meet. We'll talk inside.

204
00:18:58,000 --> 00:19:00,000
[Leol] Flutter, come in!

205
00:19:17,000 --> 00:19:20,000
I can't ever lose face
in front of Pitou.

206
00:19:20,000 --> 00:19:22,000
Well, we're gonna head back, then.

207
00:19:22,000 --> 00:19:25,000
[Leol] Wait.
Hold on a second. It's fine.

208
00:19:25,000 --> 00:19:27,000
I think I can handle it.

209
00:19:37,000 --> 00:19:39,000
At least you're both trustworthy.

210
00:19:39,000 --> 00:19:43,000
Idiots. As if I'd tell you the truth.

211
00:19:43,000 --> 00:19:45,000
[narrator]
This is Leol's rental pod.

212
00:19:45,000 --> 00:19:47,000
It's a device that allows him
to temporarily borrow

213
00:19:53,000 --> 00:19:56,000
before he can put it into action.

214
00:19:56,000 --> 00:19:59,000
First, he must have seen the ability,
or at the very least know its name.

215
00:19:59,000 --> 00:20:00,000
SATELLITE DRAGONFLIES

216
00:20:01,000 --> 00:20:07,000
Second, he must grant the target a favor
and confirm by saying, "You owe me,"

217
00:20:07,000 --> 00:20:10,000
or, "This isn't free,"
something along those lines.

218
00:20:10,000 --> 00:20:12,000
And the target
must respond affirmatively,

219
00:20:30,000 --> 00:20:31,000
[Leol] Flutter's fine.

220
00:20:31,000 --> 00:20:32,000
[Welfin chuckles]

221
00:20:32,000 --> 00:20:34,000
[Leol] He's not responding,

222
00:20:34,000 --> 00:20:38,000
because he's either unconscious,
or too far away.

223
00:20:38,000 --> 00:20:40,000
[narrator] A rental
can be used for one hour.

224
00:20:40,000 --> 00:20:41,000
During the rental period,

225
00:20:41,000 --> 00:20:44,000
the target cannot use
the borrowed power.

226
00:20:45,000 --> 00:20:47,000
[Leol] He's still alive, anyway.

227
00:20:47,000 --> 00:20:49,000
Looks like we can stay in touch.

228
00:20:54,000 --> 00:20:57,000
[Bloster] All right. We'll keep
the weaklings at a distance

229
00:20:57,000 --> 00:20:59,000
while you deal with that one.

230
00:21:21,000 --> 00:21:24,000
not until I make the King owe me one.

231
00:21:24,000 --> 00:21:29,000
[narrator] Taking the ticket
and ripping it up activates the ability.

232
00:21:31,000 --> 00:21:33,000
[Leol] They're here.

233
00:21:34,000 --> 00:21:36,000
Time to start scouting.

234
00:21:37,000 --> 00:21:41,000
[thunder rumbling]

235
00:21:41,000 --> 00:21:42,000
[King] I don't like it.

236
00:21:43,000 --> 00:21:48,000
During our matches, my rhythm
is the one being disrupted, not hers.

237
00:21:50,000 --> 00:21:54,000
By all rights, this should be
an unbearable indignity,

238
00:21:55,000 --> 00:22:00,000
and yet, although
I find myself frustrated,

239
00:22:00,000 --> 00:22:02,000
I enjoy it at the same time.

240
00:22:02,000 --> 00:22:04,000
[closing theme music playing]

241
00:22:04,000 --> 00:22:06,000
What I don't understand…

242
00:22:06,000 --> 00:22:08,000
is why.

243
00:22:10,000 --> 00:22:13,000
[singer singing in Japanese]

244
00:23:37,000 --> 00:23:39,000
-[Morel] Well…
-[Gon gulps]

245
00:23:39,000 --> 00:23:41,000
[Morel] Tonkotsu.

246
00:23:43,000 --> 00:23:47,000
[singer singing in Japanese]
